    "summary": "New src/mcp/forward-step.ts: forwardStep(tool, rawArgs, { client?, onProgress? }) opens a step.call stream to the daemon socket with params { tool, args: rawArgs, context: { cwd: process.cwd(), envRepo: INSRC_REPO when set, client } } and resolves with the 'done' frame's data unchanged. ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED (and any other socket error) -> DaemonUnreachableError (code daemon-unreachable, retryable); a plain 'unknown method: step.call' line or an error frame with code step-unknown-tool -> DaemonTooOldError (code daemon-too-old); both returned as isError envelopes in the handlers' { next:'error', error:{ code, name, message, retryable } } shape; the MCP process never runs a handler. src/mcp/server.ts: the seven step tools' registrations call forward(tool, rawArgs, extra), which converts the client name to 'claude'|'codex' and relays progress frames through the existing mcpProgressSink only when extra._meta.progressToken is set. Removed from server.ts: the imports of the step handlers, analyze-oneshot, shaper-provider and the sampling bridge, the in-process handleAnalyze body, the interim socket-client install, and from runInsrcMcpStdio the declareLiveStoreReaderUntilS11 call and the builtin tool / data driver / workflow runner registration. STEP_TOOL_NAMES moved to src/shared/step-context.ts (host.ts re-exports it). The MCP server's value-import graph now reaches 18 modules (from 523), none under src/db, src/analyze or src/daemon/steps. Tool surface: a golden file of listTools (name, title, description, inputSchema for all twelve tools) was captured through a real MCP client from the unchanged server at e30638e5, before any t9 edit, and the test compares against it. Two source scans made stale by the task were updated (permitted-reader name now only at its definition; no src/mcp file, server.ts included, imports src/daemon/steps). Falsifying mutations (a steps import in server.ts, a db import below the forwarder, refused/unknown-method/unknown-tool mappings removed, progress relayed without a token, one description edited) each fail a test. Full sweep in docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/sweeps.md.",
